  "content": {
    "id": "p34-q08-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "The coefficient of $x^2$ is double the coefficient of $x^3$ in the expansion of $(2+3x)^n$. Find the value of $n$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$n=3$\n\nUse the two binomial coefficients and simplify their ratio.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}[x^2](2+3x)^n&=\\binom{n}{2}2^{n-2}3^2\\\\{}[x^3](2+3x)^n&=\\binom{n}{3}2^{n-3}3^3\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the stated relationship,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\binom{n}{2}2^{n-2}9&=2\\binom{n}{3}2^{n-3}27\\\\\\binom{n}{2}&=3\\binom{n}{3}\\end{align*}$$\nFor $n\\ge3$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\binom{n}{3}}{\\binom{n}{2}}&=\\frac{n-2}{3}\\\\\\frac{1}{3}&=\\frac{n-2}{3}\\\\n&=3\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 78
  },
